    "result_text": "Each claim now shows its status log: one `claim-log-line` per status it has had, oldest first, as `<STATUS> by <user> on <date> due=<due>`. `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests in the spec.\n\n**Stored data**\n- A new migration, `V24__claim_log.sql`, adds a `claim_log` table. Each row holds the status, who made the change, the sheet's today at that moment and the due at that moment.\n- The due is saved as text when the line is written, so later rate or setting changes don't alter old lines.\n- Claims created before this change have no lines; nothing was backfilled for them.\n\n**Server**\n- `ClaimLog` (new) writes a log line and reads a sheet's lines back as text.\n- The due comes from a new `Rollup.figureOf(claim)`. It uses the same figure the rollup totals use (settled due, else the figure a statement bound it to, else the live due with the floor, plus any late charge), so it matches the due shown on screen.\n- A new `LogClaimStatus` step runs after the claim is saved in three places: adding a claim, quick-add (both write the DRAFT line) and the open/settle/approve/reject/void action. A settle that the clerk limit turns into PENDING is logged as PENDING.\n- Bulk open writes a line for each claim it opens. A refused change writes no line, because the step only runs once every check has passed.\n- Claim responses now carry a `log` list.\n\n**Front end**\n- `Claims.tsx` lists the log lines under each claim row.\n\nNo audit records were added, since the spec doesn't expect any.",
